{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And they said.</b> We find in the sacred language words that are of one meaning, both joined together, and one would suffice — and behold: המבלי אין קברים (is it because there are no graves), like הרק אך במשה (Numbers 12:2)." "<b>To bring us out.</b> With kamatz gadol in place of kamatz katan, like ואומר אין רואָני (Isaiah 47:10)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:23.778416384Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}